OL,3,GNorth East
OL,4,
OL,5,CThis Evening and Tonight:FGenerally
OL,6,Fdry overnight with some lengthy clear
OL,7,Fspells. Chance of some isolated
OL,8,Fshowers at first across the north and
OL,9,Fsome hill fog across the Pennines.
OL,10,FOtherwise, becoming chilly,
OL,11,Fparticularly under clear spells in the
OL,12,Fsouth.
OL,13,
OL,14,CSunday:FDry and bright initially, but
OL,15,Fbecoming cloudy and breezy through the
OL,16,Fmorning. Rain clears eastwards by the
OL,17,Fevening to leave a dry but chilly
OL,18,Fnight, with the wind easing.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
